{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/966235-what-is-the-2-0-changeling-forte","id":966235,"title":"What is the 2.0 changeling forte?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-09T08:21:51-07:00","id":966235,"title":"What is the 2.0 changeling forte?","content":"Hello everyone.<br /> <br /> I was wondering what makes 2.0 changelings stand out compared to other supernaturals in terms of game mechanics. What are their strengths, what are their weaknesses, and which parts of character creation deserve some extra attention when planning a new character concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T08:51:18-07:00","id":966255,"title":"","content":"Well, the book isn't even out yet, just teasers. But their specialty really remains the same - being tricksters. Using the entironment to your advantage, illusions, avoidance, getting in and out of locked rooms. Everything ties back into dreams and fantasy and art. I feel the game also tend to support Finesse attributes over Power, so less raw strength and more coming from the sides.<br /> <br /> Now, compared to vampires, beasts and werewolves, changelings curious have no way of directly boosting their damage modifier. Sure, they can raise effective Strength dots, but everyone else can increase the auto-damage in some way. I'm not sure on changeling enemies, but that kind of ability makes me think that going against something with high defense or healing capabilities is a losing proposition without lots of preparation before hand. I'm highly leery of direct combat as a result. Maybe playing too much Vamp and Wolf, but that's my thoughts. <br /> <br /> When making a character, I tend to find a theme and stick with it when picking abilities. Seeming, kiths, merits, Contracts and Vows are all highly synergetic and work best together when focused on said theme. At least, that's my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-09-2016, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T09:39:17-07:00","id":966280,"title":"","content":"(Note that what we've seen so far was in a playtest state so some of this may be subject to change. In particular, we know that the dream mechanics have been changed quite a bit.) <br /> <br /> Changelings are slippery. Without cold iron restraints, you can pretty much never count on keeping one captive for long. If they promise some ongoing service to a human, they can blend in with humanity almost flawlessly as long as they hold up their end of the deal. You've got to watch what you say around them too - if something can be interpreted as a statement of intent, they can hold you to it, punishing you if you don't keep to your word.<br /> <br /> Changelings are perceptive. A Changeling that manages to keep their Clarity at a decent level gets some respectable bonuses to perception-related rolls, and they have access to a wide variety of powers related to perception and revelation.<br /> <br /> Changelings are masters of dreams. Where other creatures that can enter dreams generally do so in a special dream form that alters their stats and limits their capabilities, a Changeling can literally just walk bodily into a person's dreams like they're physical spaces. Moreover, once inside a dream they can interact with it in ways rivaled only by the Horrors of the Primordial Dream, sculpting it to their hearts' desires.<br /> <br /> Changelings are master emotional manipulators. They can play you like a fiddle, making you feel however they want you to feel, and then using that emotional energy to fuel their own powers. If they're feeling especially cruel, they can drain your emotions completely dry in an instant, leaving you feeling nothing while they replenish their Glamour pool completely. <br /> <br /> Changelings are downright terrifying when they need to be. A Changeling that throws caution to the wind, Dropping the Mask, Embracing the Wyrd, and Scouring people's emotions wantonly is a goddamn force of nature.<br /> <br /> Changelings are, however, quite subtle most of the time. And breaking that subtlety comes at a huge risk. A significant amount of their capabilities are defensive in nature, dedicated to keeping them hidden from the eyes of the Gentry and their Huntsmen, protecting themselves from their pursuers, and avoiding or escaping capture. Proactivity is not really their strong point, except when it comes to preparing their defenses. And, similarly to Demons, some of their most powerful abilities attract the attention of the enemies that they are so focused on trying to stay hidden and protected from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-09-2016, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:12:11-07:00","id":970398,"title":"","content":"Several different things, but with Changeling they diverge alot depending on Kith, Contracts, Seeming, merits, and Court.<br /> <br /> But the universal one is becoming stronger in the face of things that should break them.<br /> <br /> Take a look at how Changelings deal with breaking points.<br /> <br /> Something causes a breaking point in a Changeling, so either the Changeling wins the roll and gains acuity (and one other benifical condition in the case of an exceptional sucess), which can easily be used to regain clarity or the Changeling fails that roll, and gains a condition, which can be used to gain a beat, which in turn can be traded in for an experience point.<br /> <br /> And aside from certain contracts and few other things, a Changeling's breaking points are based on personal trama and things that challenge their world view.<br /> <br /> The Changeling who seeks these things out makes him or herself more powerful, even if it means Clarity likely bounces all over the place.<br /> <br /> So clarity, including how one loses and gains it and the unique way it works makes Changelings very powerful in a very unique way that is universal to Changelings, it potentially means Changelings can grow in power very fast compared to some other templates, but at some risk and with some consquences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T10:16:11-07:00","id":975996,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know if we keep the Kith/Seemings and Court make up from 1.0 if it'll really be a drastic change? Because I really do not like how they changed up the Kith/Seemings in 2.0","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T10:22:50-07:00","id":975999,"title":"","content":"There will still be the Seasonal Courts written up for 2.0 and you can pair the kith of your choice with their 'traditional' seeming still too, so I imagine it will be quite similar if you want it to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T10:49:47-07:00","id":976013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowlost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/966235-what-is-the-2-0-changeling-forte?p=975996#post975996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know if we keep the Kith/Seemings and Court make up from 1.0 if it'll really be a drastic change? Because I really do not like how they changed up the Kith/Seemings in 2.0</div> </div> </div> </div>Should be pretty easy. Just limit Kith choice based on Seeming and use the sample Seasonal Courts.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, would you be willing to share why you dislike the changes to Kith and Seeming? To me, more options is always better, and being able to pair any Kith with any Seeming without having to use Dual-Kith is a huge positive to me, so it's hard for me to understand why someone would see it as a negative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-25-2016, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T12:08:25-07:00","id":976038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/966235-what-is-the-2-0-changeling-forte?p=976013#post976013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should be pretty easy. Just limit Kith choice based on Seeming and use the sample Seasonal Courts.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, would you be willing to share why you dislike the changes to Kith and Seeming? To me, more options is always better, and being able to pair any Kith with any Seeming without having to use Dual-Kith is a huge positive to me, so it's hard for me to understand why someone would see it as a negative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just making assumptions here, but by allowing more choice you risk eroding the Kiths' and Seemings' identities. Many people accociate trolls with big, burly brawler types. But a Fairest troll? A water spirit makes sense as an Elemental, and less so as a Beast. Some people probably prefer stricter thematics over a wider range of customization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T12:22:16-07:00","id":976046,"title":"","content":"Pledges. While any Demon can screw you with a pact, changelings can use sealings literally rope people with their own words if they aren\u00b4t careful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 09-25-2016, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T12:47:29-07:00","id":976055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/966235-what-is-the-2-0-changeling-forte?p=976038#post976038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just making assumptions here, but by allowing more choice you risk eroding the Kiths' and Seemings' identities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I can kind of see that. Personally, I never saw the identities as that rigid to begin with, maybe this was just the people I played with, but in my experience people just used Dual Kith to get the Seeming/Kith combination they wanted anyway, so you were already seeing Fairest Trolls and Beast Waterborn, they were just <i>also</i> Draconics and Swimmerswifts. This way you've got the same freedom without having to shoehorn a second Kith in if it doesn't fit the concepts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/966235-what-is-the-2-0-changeling-forte?p=976038#post976038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many people accociate trolls with big, burly brawler types. But a Fairest troll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says Fairest can't be big and burly? Heck, they can be downright brutish as long as they're also majestic. Fairest can be tyrannical kings just as much as they can be beautiful princesses. When I hear Fairest Troll, I think of this guy:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i291.photobucket.com/albums/ll291/euphoria1001/relish06.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/966235-what-is-the-2-0-changeling-forte?p=976038#post976038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A water spirit makes sense as an Elemental, and less so as a Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that one's easy. Just make them a fish person. There you go, you've got water, you've got beast, you're all set.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/30/74/d4/3074d41372b1be6648c14f56875e2d80.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Easy peasy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/966235-what-is-the-2-0-changeling-forte?p=976038#post976038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some people probably prefer stricter thematics over a wider range of customization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-25-2016, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T17:18:52-07:00","id":976181,"title":"","content":"Related: currently I am playing a Waterborn/Telluric Ogre. We all thought it was pretty weird when we started. Now we can't imagine a different pairing for Danica, because that is without a singular doubt who Danica is. I couldn't tell Danica as she is and will be in the First Edition of the game.<br /> <br /> It's not like the 1st Edition way of thinking is gone-if you pay close attention to the characters mentioned in the core when it comes out, you'll notice many of them portrayed as though they operated under those limitations. But then you have cases like my girl, where I have the groundwork for the sort of story I want to tell and to explore dynamics that previously would be denied.<br /> <br /> Newer players might have some trouble with the freedom that comes under this system, but this is part of the reason why there's a sidebar the size of a page that gives players a tool to simplify their choices. Older players still has the conceptions of 1E to help direct their decisions while having the freedom to deviate from that model.<br /> <br /> I can see the problem, and it's a problem that won't go away, no matter what tools are provided-but the benefits more than make up for the places where it is invariably &quot;too much&quot;.<br /> <br /> In relation, there were several forumites who felt that the wide variety of choices of kiths in 1E per seeming was going to be a severe impediment to character creation and plot design at the game's release, an argument that had pretty much died out until this update. I wonder, in the years to come, if people will still be complaining about how wide the customization is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":".  Overestimated bits of conversation I heard. Whoops. 09-26-2016, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T18:08:29-07:00","id":976200,"title":"","content":"I think the forte of Changelings is really pain = power, things that are or could be painful to them in some sense is source or opportunity for them as can be dealing with that pain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:40:44-07:00","id":976326,"title":"","content":"Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Yes, this is exactly why I don't like the new set up. CtL 1.0 was almost perfect and aside from needing a rules update the setting was fine. The changes made to it tarnish it so much so me and my friends are trying to make sure everything we loved from 1.0 is salvagable while embracing the rules from 2.0. Which we love as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/966235-what-is-the-2-0-changeling-forte?p=976038#post976038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just making assumptions here, but by allowing more choice you risk eroding the Kiths' and Seemings' identities. Many people accociate trolls with big, burly brawler types. But a Fairest troll? A water spirit makes sense as an Elemental, and less so as a Beast. Some people probably prefer stricter thematics over a wider range of customization.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T22:28:34-07:00","id":976359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/966235-what-is-the-2-0-changeling-forte?p=976038#post976038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many people accociate trolls with big, burly brawler types. But a Fairest troll?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/VYyvSoh.png\" target=\"_blank\">Example 1</a>, <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/QHUX3vB.png\" target=\"_blank\">example 2</a>. In fact, I've been wanting to make something like Dreaming Trolls for a while.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/966235-what-is-the-2-0-changeling-forte?p=976038#post976038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A water spirit makes sense as an Elemental, and less so as a Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>A merfolk or siren who is of the water but just as much about the raw animal passion of it, for an example, or a fish-person driven to follow the currents of life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/966235-what-i